  "report_discrepancies": [],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds (accrual business-type), same choices as FY2023. Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (Total Governmental Funds, p4). Roll-forward on fund balance: 808,490 + 1,822,250 - 1,462,785 - 1,838 net transfers (Total column 'Transfers from (to) other funds' (1,838)) = 1,166,117. Beginning/ending cash left null as in FY2023/FY2024 (no single governmental cash total; p3 prints cash and cash equivalents 1,152,322 and county treasurer cash 13,795 separately). Proprietary cash flows (p7) not recorded, as in FY2023/FY2024; it shows capital debt proceeds 2,990,000 and principal paid 2,991,177 (refinancing) that are not on the operating statement. Business-type (Combined System Utilities Fund) from the proprietary statement p6: 737,830 + 729,806 - 869,246 + transfers in 1,838 = 600,228; disbursements 869,246 = Statement of Activities expenses (p2). The trimmed Statement of Activities (p2) shows only the expenses / charges / operating grants columns (the general revenues and net position part is not in the trim). Detail: the trim holds only the first page of the General Fund departmental combining statement (p11: General and Police columns); the second page (Park, Enhancement, Christmas in Fort Calhoun) is not in the trim. So General Fund expenditures are taken from the combining statement for General and Police (object lines; they equal the budget schedule's General government 319,348 and Police protection 130,086) and from the budget schedule (p8) for the three environment and leisure departments (not itemized); General Fund revenues and transfers come from the budget schedule (p8) because the combining revenue lines for the missing departments are not in the trim. Street (p9) and Sales Tax (p10) budget schedules recorded; Debt Service and Lottery funds have no schedule in the trim; no business-type schedule. Zero-actual budget lines (Street motor vehicle) not recorded. 'Bond and loan proceeds' printed among revenues is a receipt line. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}
